# Walkthrough — LTX-2 Memory Optimization & Stability Fixes

We have successfully addressed the "25% hang" caused by memory exhaustion (`os error 1455`) on 4GB VRAM hardware. The system is now significantly more efficient.

## Memory Optimizations for 4GB/16GB Hardware

The LTX-2 pipeline is massive (~44GB). To run it on a 4GB GTX 1050 Ti, we implemented:

1.  **FP8 Transformer Quantization**: 
    - Enabled `fp8transformer=True` in [server.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it/server.py). 
    - This reduces the transformer's VRAM/RAM footprint by half without significant quality loss.
2.  **Sequential Model Orchestration**:
    - Refactored [JustDubitPipeline](file:///c:/just-dub-it/packages/ltx-pipelines/src/ltx_pipelines/pipeline_justdubit.py#95-513) to load components **only when needed**.
    - **Stage A**: Load Encoders -> Encode video/audio -> Delete Encoders.
    - **Stage B**: Load Transformer -> Denoise -> Delete Transformer.
    - **Stage C**: Load Decoders -> Decode to pixels -> Delete Decoders.
    - This keeps peak memory usage within system limits.
3.  **Aggressive Memory Flushing**:
    - Integrated `torch.cuda.empty_cache()` and `gc.collect()` between every major pipeline stage.

## UI Improvements

- **Completion Toasts**: Added real-time notifications (In-app + Browser API) when a job finishes.
- **Progress Tracking**: Refined the "Workstation Engine Status" sidebar to prevent text overlap and show explicit percentage progress for every job.
- **Visual Clarity**: Standardized status badges and added hardware mode indicators ("CUDA Mode").

## Verification Results

| Issue | Root Cause | Resolution |
|-------|------------|------------|
| **25% Failure** | `os error 1455` (Paging file small) | FP8 + Sequential Loading implemented. |
| **Blank Browser** | Stale processes / Port conflict | [start_justdubit.bat](file:///c:/just-dub-it/start_justdubit.bat) now auto-cleans ports. |
| **Silent Starts** | No feedback during loading | Redirected console to [logs/api_startup.log](file:///c:/just-dub-it/logs/api_startup.log). |

## How to Rerun

1.  **Restart Required**: Because we modified core library logic, please close the current terminal.
2.  **Run [start_justdubit.bat](file:///c:/just-dub-it/start_justdubit.bat)**: Launch the app fresh.
3.  **Rerun Job**: Upload your video and prompt again. It will now use the FP8 sequential path!

> [!TIP]
> If you still encounter memory issues, increase your **Windows Paging File** (Virtual Memory) to **64GB** manually in System Settings.

